.TH SIA 1
.SH NAME
sia \- talk to the assistant
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sia
.RI [ question ...]
.br
.B sia new
.RI [ question ...]
.br
.B sia resume
.I n
.br
.B sia list
|
.B forget
.IR n | all
.br
.B sia memory
.RB [ forget
.I n
|
.BR clear ]
.br
.B sia remember
.I fact
.br
.B sia info
.br
.B sia config
.IB key = value
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sia
talks to the assistant,
.BR siad (4),
which runs a language model on this machine or asks an OpenAI-compatible
service. With a
.IR question ,
it shows one answer as it is written, in your last conversation. Without,
it holds a conversation: one message per line
.RB ( you> ),
an empty line ends it.
.PP
When sia ends an answer with a line
.BI [remember: " ..." ] ,
.B sia
asks "keep it? [y/N]": nothing is remembered without your OK.
Conversations and facts are kept by siad in
.IR /var/sia/ uid ,
which only siad reads: a user only ever reaches their own memory.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR new " [\fIquestion\fP...]"
The same, in a new conversation.
.TP
.BI resume " n"
Continue conversation
.IR n .
.TP
.B list
Your saved conversations: number, turns, about how many tokens, the first
question.
.TP
.BR forget " \fIn\fP | " all
Delete conversation
.IR n ,
or all of them.
.TP
.B memory
What sia remembers about you, numbered.
.TP
.BI "memory forget" " n\fR, " "memory clear"
Remove fact
.IR n ,
or all of them.
.TP
.BI remember " fact"
Add a fact (at most 2 KB of them in all).
.TP
.B info
The backend (local or remote, ready or not), the model, the context, the
conversations open, its memory, the speed of the last answer.
.TP
.BI config " key" = value
(root) Change a setting in
.I /etc/sia.conf
(the API key goes to
.IR /etc/sia.key );
the assistant restarts with it. Keys:
.B backend=local
or
.BR remote ,
.BI model= /models/x.gguf\fR,
.BI ctx= n\fR,
.BI threads= n\fR,
.BI url= https://.../v1\fR,
.BI api_model= name\fR,
.BI api_key= key\fR,
and
.BR memory ,
.BR compact_at ,
.BR keep_turns ,
.BR max_convs ,
.BR max_log_kb ,
.BR remote_ctx .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0, or 1 on a failure (no model, the remote model unreachable, not root...).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /models
The models
.RB ( .gguf );
with no
.BR model= ,
the 1.7B one, or the first one there.
.TP
.I /etc/sia.conf
The settings
.RI ( key = value
lines).
.TP
.I /etc/sia.key
The remote service's API key (root only).
.TP
.I /var/sia/
Each user's conversations and facts (only siad's).
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
sia what is a microkernel?
sia config backend=remote
sia config url=https://api.example.com/v1
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR siad (4),
.BR svc (8)
.SH BUGS
Summaries and offered facts are only as good as the model. One warm cache
only: a conversation continued after another one was used is read again.
Root can read every user's memory.
